The synopsis: &#x201C; The Popinjay Cavalier is a rambunctious comedy of deception and disguise inspired by the grand swashbuckling epics of stage and screen. A sweeping celebration of theatre and its heightened romance, told with Tarantino&#x2019;s signature style and unmistakable wit.&#x201D;

The creative team joining Tarantino includes: Scenic and Costume Design by Tom Pye; Lighting Design by Natasha Chivers; Sound Design by Ian Dickinson for Autograph Sound; Fight Direction by Philip d&#x2019;Orleans; Action Co-ordination by Sam Lyon-Behan; Music by Tim Phillips; Casting by Jim Carnahan and Alexandre Bleu, CSA; and Associate Direction by Jack Bradfield.

EXCLUSIVE : Following its world premiere in the Cannes Classics program and official selection at Telluride, Maverick: The Epic Adventures of David Lean has sold to key territories for Embankment Films.

MetFilm Distribution is releasing the film in the UK & Ireland from December 4, and deals have been secured with ARTE ZDF in France & Germany, A Contracorriente in Spain, and Limelight in Australia & New Zealand. Sky has UK broadcast rights.

Written and directed by Barnaby Thompson and narrated by Cate Blanchett, Kenneth Branagh provides the voice of Lean. Contributors include Steven Spielberg, Wes Anderson, Celine Song, Paul Greengrass, Joe Wright, Nia Da Costa, Alfonso Cuaron, Autumn Durald Arkapaw, Francis Ford Coppola, Brady Corbet, Steven Soderbergh and Denis Villeneuve. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Documentary David Lean Returns To Cannes In 'Maverick' Documentary, Exploring How Director Overcame Father's Scorn To Become One Of Cinema's Greatest News Doha Film Festival Lifts Off As Gulf States Remain On High Alert Amid Iran Strikes

One of cinema's greats, Lean's singular vision and dogged determination to film the impossible earned him the reputation of an obsessive maverick. Starting out in news editing, Lean went on to become film editor to celebrated British filmmakers Michael Powell and Emeric Pressberger and collaborator of Noel Coward, before embarking on his own 17-strong movie-making legacy, featuring iconic films as Brief Encounter, Oliver Twist, The Bridge on the River Kwai, Lawrence of Arabia, Doctor Zhivago, Ryan's Daughter and A Passage to India . Despite being a creator of the epic on screen, his own personal life remained messy, rootless and painful. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

The film is produced by Embankment Films, Fragile Films and Assemble Media.

Producer Jack Heller said: &#x201C;We are delighted to have MetFilm on board for the UK & Ireland theatrical release, who will release the film in select cinemas in advance of Sky&#x2019;s broadcast premiere. We were always intent on making a feature documentary about David Lean worthy of the big screen, and are immensely grateful to Sky for supporting this endeavour.&#x201D;

Imax has locked a deal with Showcase Cinemas to install 13 new Imax with Laser systems across 12 locations in the United Kingdom and one additional European location, the largest deal the company has completed in the UK.

The deal was announced in a statement by Imax, which also revealed that former Cineworld CEO Mooky Greidinger has acquired Showcase Cinemas. Greidinger left Cineworld in 2023 following a restructure after a Chapter 11 bankruptcy process in the United States.

As part of this deal, five new Imax locations will open across the UK in 2027, with the remaining sites opening over the next few years. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Imax Ups Giovanni Dolci To Newly Created COO Role, Mark Welton To Head Strategic Partnerships News Imax CEO Wades Into 'Cliff Booth' Debate: "Frankly, I Don't Understand"

&#x201C;Mooky is a visionary leader and an excellent partner who recognized the value in IMAX long before our recent run of record-breaking success &#x2014; we&#x2019;re excited to be back in business with his team at Showcase Cinemas UK,&#x201D; Rich Gelfond, CEO of IMAX, said in a statement. &#x201C;This agreement significantly expands our footprint in one of our most successful markets, and underscores the strong opportunity for network growth as we deliver our best year ever at the global box office.&#x201D; Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Greidinger added: &#x201C;I&#x2019;ve been in the IMAX business for decades, and the value of its technology, brand, and strategic partnership to exhibitors have grown exponentially in that time. There is no doubt that IMAX plays a significant role in the results of the industry and I am sure it will continue to grow and attract new audiences and become even more significant in the coming years. I look forward to working with Rich and his team and making the IMAX Experience a cornerstone of the new Showcase Cinemas in the UK.&#x201D;

Earlier this week, Imax confirmed longtime exec Giovanni Dolci has been promoted to a newly created role of chief operating officer, overseeing the company&#x2019;s expanding global theater network.

One of the key promises David Ellison made to the industry in the lead-up to his heavily scrutinized merger of Paramount and Warner Brothers was that the newly-formed Skydance would release at least 30 films theatrically per year . To ensure that he delivers on the promise, the studio magnate will need to look beyond Hollywood, said top entertainment business investor Joe Ravitch .

Ravitch, who is the co-founder and partner of the Raine Group , a global merchant bank focused exclusively on technology, media and telecommunications, gave an insightful keynote talk on the first day of the Doha Film Festival &#x2019;s Industry Days. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Oscar Predictions: Documentary Feature — Will the Branch Embrace ‘You Can See Everything’ or Snub the Frontrunner (Again)? Oscar Predictions: Best Casting — 'Being Heumann' and 'La Bola Negra' Found the Year's Boldest Discoveries. Will the Academy Reward Them?

&#x201C;Paramount-Warner is committing to 30 theatrical releases a year,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;I would guarantee you they are going to need international films to succeed as part of the world plan for national releases. And those are big investments by them. They are going to be looking to the world and partners to help feed that pipeline across multiple genres.&#x201D;

Ravitch cited this gap as one of the key opportunities contributing to a golden window for Arab cinema to fulfill its international potential. Another, even more pressing one, is the streamers&#x2019; growing interest in the Global South after having exhausted their subscriber base in the Western world, particularly Netflix . Last month, the major platform&#x2019;s shares hit a two-year low , with the concerning numbers coming a few days after a massive round of layoffs that saw the American powerhouse dismiss key executives such as chief content officer Bela Bajaria and film chief Dan Lin.

&#x201C;The next wave for the streamers is the Global South,&#x201D; said Ravitch. &#x201C;Netflix stock is down. Why? Because they&#x2019;ve basically matured and have hit [all] subscription levels they&#x2019;re ever going to hit in Western Europe and the United States. They are focused on Asia; they are focused on Africa, the Middle East. The same is true for all the streamers. That&#x2019;s where they see subscriber growth happening, so that&#x2019;s where they need to get into that kind of content.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

This movement is even more interesting to Arab execs given that streamers are flocking to the region at a time when the &#x201C;Hollywood monoculture is over,&#x201D; he noted, adding how films like "Avengers: Doomsday" and "The Odyssey" will always top global box office charts, but "the next 10 films in a particular market are going to be local, and the streamers know that,&#x201D; said the veteran. &#x201C;If all the streamers show up in a market and deliver Hollywood content, they are not going to succeed.&#x201D;

The world of tentpoles, Ravitch noted, is also eroding. Getting &#x201C;big stars&#x201D; to do &#x201C;superhero movies&#x201D; based on IP is no longer the easiest route to success in Hollywood. &#x201C;We&#x2019;ve seen this through &#x2018;Backrooms,&#x2019; &#x2018;Obsession,&#x2019; and other small-budget, YouTube movies succeeding beyond anybody&#x2019;s wildest imagination. That&#x2019;s a trend that will continue.&#x201D;

The end of an era of over-reliance on stars is pivotal to the Middle East&#x2019;s strategy to internationalize its industry, given that many countries in the region have opted to kickstart their markets by attracting big-gun Hollywood names either to shoot in their territory or promote it as a destination. &#x201C;I think there have been a lot of missteps, to be honest,&#x201D; said Ravitch of the strategy, refusing to cite any countries as an example of such practice. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s not about getting Tom Cruise to shoot a movie,&#x201D; he observed.

&#x201C;There&#x2019;s been too much of a race to the bottom historically of 'let&#x2019;s get a famous movie star to come shoot this movie here' as opposed to a sort of bottom-up approach,&#x201D; he continued. This strategy is inefficient because the Hollywood films shot in Arab countries tend to be generic, characterless representations of the region that lead audiences to believe they might have been shot elsewhere.

Audiences can just as easily believe films have been shot in other popular production hubs such as Hungary, Italy and China, added the exec.

"[Productions] will go wherever it&#x2019;s cheapest to shoot the film,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;It doesn&#x2019;t develop any kind of organic organization or systematized way where people are going to [focus] on the local culture.&#x201D;

Focusing on developing local creativity, while also feeding from the know-how of international execs is the strongest way forward, especially in a market that has a key advantage: demand driven by a native audience coupled with demand from streamers. &#x201C;What&#x2019;s exciting to me about Arab culture, having done this in China, Korea, India and other places, is that you actually have a market here,&#x201D; Ravitch pointed out. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;Whether it&#x2019;s the Arab diaspora or Arab-speaking markets, there&#x2019;s real disposable income and a common culture,&#x201D; he said. The Arab world is a huge market, with around 500 million Arabic speakers worldwide, including a significant diasporic population in the U.S. and Europe, who also want to see themselves and their culture represented on screen.

There is, however, one key issue: streamers have famously entered international markets without sharing creative rights or long-term revenue with local makers. Industries in massive markets like Brazil, Netflix&#x2019;s second-largest subscriber base, have been trying to regulate streamers for years without success.

Sitting in the audience, chairman and chief executive officer of AGC Studio Stuart Ford asked Ravitch about this &#x201C;wrinkle in the system,&#x201D; which he described as: &#x201C;Streaming doesn't share in the revenues. So ultimately you have local sectors and local stakeholders such as the Film Committee [in Qatar] [who] will invest in local content, develop it, finance it, but ultimately, if they want the global audience as the industry stands today, they're gonna give up most of the upside.&#x201D;

Stuart brought up the case of &#x201C;Squid Game.&#x201D; The massively popular series skyrocketed Korean production company Firstman Studio to global prominence, but Netflix owns the rights to the franchise. &#x201C;They gave away the goose that laid the golden egg,&#x201D; said Ravitch.

&#x201C;One of my good friends at Property Media has a top show on Apple, one of the top shows on Paramount, and he makes no money because he got 120% cost,&#x201D; he added. &#x201C;So he'll never make any. That's a systemic problem we have.&#x201D;

&#x201C;As we start at the infancy of really building the more mature market for Arab storytelling and Arab culture, it's something to be thoughtful about and careful about in how to avoid that and how to create an environment where all the streamers sort of want to be in this market.&#x201D;

"I'm sure Julia Roberts or Jennifer Lawrence don't constantly answer questions about Trump or Marion Cotillard about Marion Le Pen!&#x201D; Speaking Thursday at the Black Nights Film Festival (P&#xD6;FF) panel &#x201C;Women, War and Witness: Cinema in Times of Global Crisis,&#x201D; Iranian-born star Golshifteh Farahani (&#x201C;Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Men Tell No Tales&#x201D;) didn&#x2019;t mince her words about politics, who controls the narrative and cinema.

Farahani is attending the festival with &#x201C; When She Hears the Bells ,&#x201D; which is competing for best first feature. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Oscars: International Feature — ‘La Bola Negra,’ ‘Fjord’ and 'Minotaur' Lead Early Contenders John Turturro on Nearly Robbing Someone to Practice for 'The Only Living Pickpocket in New York,' Fighting to Save His 2005 Musical 'Romance & Cigarettes' and the Knicks Championship

Sitting alongside Farahani during the panel was Halkawt Mustafa , Norwegian-Kurdish writer, director and producer of the film &#x201C; No Paradise if You Are Killed By a Woman ,&#x201D; Iraq&#x2019;s Oscar hopeful and earlier Venice out-of-competition entry, which will receive on Nov. 20 P&#xD6;FF&#x2019;s first ever Free World Award, backed by the Ukrainian State Agency.

Sharing the discussion on Zoom with Mustafa and Farahani were Natalia Libel from Ukraine-based 2Brave Productions; and Mariia Vynogradova and Ksenia Bugrimova, co-founders of Talented U and the Women and the World International Film Festival.

Asked by moderator and Egyptian journalist Ahmed Sahwky if, as an international actor from Iran, she felt split between focusing on her art or discussing her country at war in the media, Farahani immediately hit back. &#x201C;I'm sure Julia Roberts or Jennifer Lawrence don't constantly answer questions about Trump or Marion Cotillard about Marion Le Pen,&#x201D; she said. &#x201C;I would have loved to sit here and talk about cinema, but I'm always questioned unnecessarily about politics, because politics today are so polarized. It&#x2019;s either black or white, and if you are neither of them, in the middle, you cannot exist. It&#x2019;s very dangerous because harmony comes from the middle.&#x201D; Despite her quick digression, Farahani said she loved being &#x201C;Yazidi women, Kurdish women, Afghan women, Lebanese women&#x201D; on screen. &#x201C;I somehow lived through this region of war; I can feel the suffering because of this black gold in the region that we are living in, unfortunately, or fortunately.&#x201D;

Bouncing back on the question of women, war and cinema, Farahani said &#x201C;if you're coming from a country at war like Ukraine, you become that country&#x2019;s representative, your individuality is taken away from you, as you need to be a flagship [of that country].&#x201D; Mustafa concurred, saying he's been asked which flag he should raise, the Kurdish or Iraqi one, and if he shouldn&#x2019;t have a Norwegian perspective with &#x201C;No Paradise if You Are Killed By a Woman,&#x201D; screening at Tallinn&#x2019;s Best of Festivals&#x2019; section. Yet all that mattered for him was to draw with this film a portrait of a Kurdish woman, to remain as true as possible to her perspective, the one of a Kurdish Peshmerga sniper returning to the battlefield to rescue her younger sister from ISIS captivity.

For Farahani, who has spent 20 years in exile in France, it is people&#x2019;s prejudice or distorted views of a person, living in a country at war, which is a heavy weight to carry. &#x201C;People enjoy &#x201C;victimizing you and say, oh, poor Ukrainian people with the war. Oh, it must be so horrible in Iran. When you are in certain positions, you have to be in that box, and you're not allowed to exist in that box. So not only are you imprisoned by bombs, war and oppressive regimes, you're imprisoned by the world that is putting you in that box!&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Farahani who first gained international recognition for her role in &#x201C;The Pear Tree,&#x201D; had to leave Iran in 2008 after backlashes with local authorities following her appearance in Ridley Scott's Hollywood film &#x201C;Body of Lies.&#x201D;

Answering Sahwky&#x2019;s question about an artist&#x2019;s moral dilemma regarding what project to board or not, she said once in the West, she had to fight new challenges about stereotypes. "When I left Iran, it was the time Bush was calling Iran [part of] the axis of evil," she told the audience in Tallinn. &#x201C;I went to America, and all the parts that I was reading were either terrorists, or about someone involved in some terrorist action, or about some underground party scene in Tehran.&#x201D;

She said coming from Iran, she could not accept any of those parts, despite being in a precarious financial situation. Still to this day, she sticks to her guts, her truthfulness, her dignity. &#x201C;It's just absolute bullshit what Hollywood shows of our region. It's propaganda from the U.S., propaganda from Iran; we are victims of propaganda from both sides,&#x201D; she complained. But what about filmmakers, forced to fit into the system and exert self-censorship to be able to work? asked Sahwky, himself well aware of the pressures on artists from Egyptian authorities. &#x201C;It comes down to Hollywood, writing and rewriting history," Farahani said. "White supremacy [at U.S. studios], them deciding, giving money, writing and rewriting history.&#x201D; Vynogradova said her platform, Talented U, was contributing to change and helping filmmakers from countries at war. &#x201C;We just give them an opportunity to be heard, to be seen, this is our main thing.&#x201D;

Bugrimova said more responsibility should be on the producers, the industry or on bigger film festivals, which should &#x201C;not just be a platform. They should make a difference for the filmmakers selected, coming from war zones, help them to find the right person in the room or help them spread the word [against war].&#x201D; Free World Award

